# The trigger needs combat damage to a *player* (CR 510.2, 702.19b) and a target artifact that player controls. Mother
# of Runes attacks into two Ornithopters that double-block, and the Ire makes her a 3/3 trampler: two to the first
# Ornithopter, one to the second, none left for Bot2 (lethal must be assigned to every blocker before the player,
# CR 702.19b), so there is no damage to the player and the trigger never happens: Bot2's Sol Ring survives and no target
# is asked for. The Ire's effects end at cleanup, so on turn five Mother has no trample.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mother of Runes
Dreadmaw's Ire
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Sol Ring
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Mother of Runes > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter#1 > Mother of Runes; Ornithopter#2 > Mother of Runes)
[T3 Bot1.Blockers]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dreadmaw's Ire.Cast(Mother of Runes)
! Bot1.Target
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Ornithopter; Sol Ring
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Keywords = (absent)

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Dreadmaw's Ire
